I've ascended Nethack games before (2 Knights, 1 Valkyrie) but I just
finished my first SLASH'EM ascension- never polymorphed an object, but
that was the only conduct I was able to ascend with- my main focus was
on succeeding rather than conducts. Quite a smooth game all in all,
had to use up one amulet of lifesaving on a rather careless situation
(purple worm plucked me off my ki-rin over water on the Medusa level,
lost my saddle, my ki-rin, and used up an AoLS, but everything was
easily replacable. The only other serious hiccup came in Moloch's
Sanctum on another careless play, Excalibur got plucked from my hand
by a bullwhip and I didn't pick it up instantly- conflict was on and
its new owner was petrified in the shuffle, and I didn't have a
pickaxe or wand of striking on me, and my knowledge of Stone to Flesh
was stale! I still had my Wand of Wishing from the castle charged
however, and after clearing the foyer with my lance/saber I was able
to burn a wish to extricate my sword from its stony imprisonment and
continue on.

I've been attempting SLASH'EM for a couple of years now off and on- at
first I was taken aback at how much more difficult it was than vanilla
nethack, but I've grown quite accustomed to it by now. I remember the
first breakthrough slash game I had; I was too confident in my own
preparedness and challenged Vecna prematurely. I was left staring at
"Do you want your possessions identified?", slowly realizing that I
had a lot to learn before I made it. Time really taught me the
patience necessary to succeed- even though I made a couple careless
mistakes in this one, I was very patient in going up and down,
extracting everything of value I could besides pudding farming/
polypiling before making my final run.

While I'm here, I might as well pose a question- The Wizard cursed my
saddle while I was riding on the Plane of Earth- I subsequently used
Conflict throughout the Planes and was never thrown from my mount.
Does having a cursed saddle mean a Conflict-addled mount will not
throw you off?

In any case, I think I'll try Undead Hunter next- maybe I'll be making
YAAP about him/her at some point too.


